   "claims": [
    "This specification determines the arrow speed, provided that you keep the following parameters: Draw length equal to 30 inches; Draw weight equal to 70 pounds; and Arrow weighing 350 grains.",
    "Archery calculator principles You should adjust the arrow speed given by the IBO specification according to the following rules: For every inch of draw length under 30″, subtract 10 ft/s from the IBO value.",
    "For every 3 grains of total arrow weight above draw weight multiplied by 5, subtract 1 ft/s from the IBO value.",
    "These are calculated as follows: momentum = 𝐴 ⋅ 𝑣 kinetic energy = 𝐴 ⋅ 𝑣 2 2 momentumkinetic energy​=A⋅v=2A⋅v2​​ Our arrow speed calculator converts the units automatically.",
    "Let's say you keep the regular peak draw weight of 70 lbs but use arrows weighing 400 grains.",
    "Use the following method: Fire a group of arrows from 20 yards using the pin set for this distance.",
    "Change the distance to 40 yards and shoot another group of arrows to the same pin you used from 20 yards.",
    "If you are using a recurve bow, arrows can travel at up to 225 feet per second (fps) or 150mph, while arrows from a compound bow travel at up to 300 fps (200mph).",
    "For example, if you increase the draw weight by 5 pounds the speed of your arrows can increase by 10 fps."
   ],
